WEBVTT

00:31.114 --> 00:33.950
THE TRUNK

00:34.034 --> 00:38.121
LATE SO HYE-YEONG

01:17.452 --> 01:20.121
This is a pretty lonely
memorial service, huh?

01:24.334 --> 01:26.252
I'm so sorry to leave you by yourself.

01:28.421 --> 01:29.964
Next time we see each other…

01:31.966 --> 01:33.927
I won't dare to leave your side, okay?

01:38.848 --> 01:40.391
I will not leave you alone.

01:49.734 --> 01:51.152
Was anyone else there?

01:51.945 --> 01:52.779
Mm-hmm.

01:53.655 --> 01:55.031
I know you're lying.

01:55.740 --> 01:58.326
We're all Hye-yeong's got.
Who else would come?

01:59.994 --> 02:01.538
I'm sorry I couldn't make it.

02:02.539 --> 02:05.041
Well, it's not like
you skipped it on purpose.

02:06.793 --> 02:07.877
It's all right.

02:50.879 --> 02:53.339
YEONHEE UNIVERSITY
GRADUATION GOWN AND CAP RENTALS

03:31.920 --> 03:33.171
Did someone die?

03:37.634 --> 03:38.551
Friend of mine.

03:40.178 --> 03:43.139
I thought traditional hairpins
were for family funerals.

03:48.228 --> 03:49.938
I wore them 'cause she had no one.

03:51.272 --> 03:53.024
And it feels like I got her killed.

03:54.609 --> 03:55.610
How about you?

03:59.155 --> 04:00.240
It was my mother.

04:06.037 --> 04:07.789
I feel like I killed her too.

04:31.729 --> 04:32.647
I'm sure

04:33.982 --> 04:35.650
you're not the reason she died.

04:46.077 --> 04:48.997
HAN JEONG-WON

04:49.080 --> 04:55.003
THE TRUNK

06:31.349 --> 06:32.433
Are you all right?

06:34.644 --> 06:36.521
Uh, it's not my blood.

06:38.106 --> 06:39.357
How did you know where to go?

06:40.483 --> 06:42.485
The contract says
it's your listed address.

06:59.001 --> 07:00.753
Did Eom Tae-seong come here before?

07:02.213 --> 07:03.631
Is this your fiancé's place?

07:04.799 --> 07:06.008
The guy your mom ruined.

07:09.804 --> 07:11.139
And why do you care about that?

07:13.641 --> 07:15.601
Um, I was just concerned.

07:15.685 --> 07:17.228
You should go. Don't worry about it.

07:17.728 --> 07:19.397
This has nothing to do with you,
Jeong-won.

07:21.357 --> 07:23.734
We're together.
I'm not allowed to be concerned?

07:24.569 --> 07:25.778
You're my wife, aren't you?

07:29.073 --> 07:30.616
You think this is special, what we have?

07:33.578 --> 07:35.329
You're immature. That hasn't changed.

07:35.830 --> 07:36.873
Very selfish.

07:38.291 --> 07:39.917
You have always been particular.

07:42.587 --> 07:44.630
At the end of the day,
this is still a job.

07:44.714 --> 07:46.466
This is all straight from the manual.

07:46.549 --> 07:49.010
I cooked for you in the morning
and grilled the fish

07:49.093 --> 07:52.555
so you'd have some sort of order
in your home and routine.

07:53.139 --> 07:55.057
So can you honor my boundaries?

07:57.018 --> 07:59.854
Do you take pleasure
in playing the role of the ideal wife?

08:00.730 --> 08:03.357
You're stuck in someone's house,
and you can't leave.

08:04.358 --> 08:06.486
Do you take pride in helping
sad-sack guys like me?

08:06.569 --> 08:08.571
That's how you wash away the remorse?

08:10.072 --> 08:12.742
You've been going along
with all of it too, Jeong-won.

08:14.160 --> 08:17.705
And that is why you didn't have to come
all this way just to play the hero.

08:18.789 --> 08:20.750
So just stay out of my life, will you?

08:21.959 --> 08:25.129
And if Eom Tae-seong comes around or not,
it's none of your business.

08:28.049 --> 08:30.468
This isn't your space,
and I think you should go.

08:31.969 --> 08:33.679
Right, it's not your space either.

08:36.432 --> 08:38.059
You've been clinging to your ex.

08:39.060 --> 08:41.270
You're afraid of who you'll be
if you let go.

08:47.193 --> 08:49.028
But you don't have to be afraid.

08:51.864 --> 08:54.158
Are you afraid
you might actually fall for me?

09:01.415 --> 09:02.333
Come on, now.

09:03.501 --> 09:05.294
Go hide in your lavish mansion.

09:55.595 --> 09:57.763
Hi. Welcome.

09:57.847 --> 10:00.182
Rubbing alcohol, iodine.
I need antiseptics.

10:00.266 --> 10:02.685
Uh, painkillers, ban… bandages.

10:02.768 --> 10:04.186
Everything. Strong drugs.

10:04.687 --> 10:06.606
Uh, how did you get injured, sir?

10:06.689 --> 10:09.525
Oh, well, ya know… screwdriver stabbing.

10:10.026 --> 10:13.112
I think you need
to go to the ER tonight, sir.

10:13.195 --> 10:17.199
Oh, this bitch. She is un-fucking-real.

10:21.370 --> 10:24.832
Uh, just… would you hand it over?

10:42.224 --> 10:43.976
You sure have changed a lot.

10:44.477 --> 10:46.103
Mr. Seo is scary.

10:47.229 --> 10:49.315
This is so out of character for you.

10:51.108 --> 10:52.068
You did this.

10:53.152 --> 10:54.528
You turned me into this.

10:55.154 --> 10:56.489
You think I wouldn't find out

10:57.573 --> 10:58.991
what you did five years ago?

11:01.160 --> 11:03.496
So you think
I was the one who sent the videos?

11:04.955 --> 11:06.874
It was her own mother who did it.

11:06.957 --> 11:09.627
All I was doing was acting
in the public interest, telling her.

11:10.127 --> 11:11.462
Wait.

11:12.004 --> 11:13.255
If you were to die,

11:14.340 --> 11:16.050
all I'd have to do is disappear again.

11:16.550 --> 11:18.386
So if you ever show yourself again, I'll…

11:19.470 --> 11:20.554
I will ruin you.

11:42.535 --> 11:43.869
Come on, ma'am.

11:44.453 --> 11:47.164
You really think I'm gonna hurt you?

11:47.248 --> 11:49.125
I mean, look at me.
I'm in pain.

11:53.170 --> 11:54.213
Listen, bitch.

11:56.424 --> 11:58.551
You think I'll hurt you?

12:02.722 --> 12:03.764
Damn it.

12:13.274 --> 12:14.817
The stuff won't come off.

12:15.359 --> 12:18.738
Yeah. To be honest,
the situation isn't ideal.

12:19.989 --> 12:21.240
Right, I understand.

12:22.783 --> 12:24.618
Wait. Hang up, hang up, hang up.

12:37.631 --> 12:39.383
Whose blood is on my floor?

12:41.385 --> 12:43.471
Holy shit. It is you, after all.

12:45.389 --> 12:47.057
I can't believe we're meeting.

12:48.726 --> 12:51.437
I'm Ms. Do-dam. I live next door.

12:51.520 --> 12:52.563
I know In-ji well.

12:52.646 --> 12:55.149
I know she's sat in there for five years,
drowning in sadness.

12:58.027 --> 13:00.029
Was this a regular thing?

13:00.112 --> 13:02.239
Took your time showing up.
Why not wait till she's dead?

13:02.323 --> 13:04.241
You might as well.
God, give me a fucking break.

13:06.660 --> 13:08.370
I've heard Tae-seong's been

13:08.454 --> 13:11.749
stalking In-ji and harassing her
in all kinds of messed-up ways.

13:12.708 --> 13:14.543
I heard the son of a bitch killed someone.

13:28.474 --> 13:29.642
God help me.

13:30.726 --> 13:31.936
Driving me nuts.

15:07.907 --> 15:09.783
Manual, my ass, huh.

15:20.711 --> 15:23.255
Having strawberries
used to feel like a luxury,

15:23.756 --> 15:25.341
but now I just eat them like candy.

15:29.094 --> 15:31.138
I just can't help myself. I swear.

15:34.975 --> 15:36.393
He told me I should do it.

15:37.686 --> 15:39.897
In exchange, he wants nothing
to do with the child.

15:40.648 --> 15:42.816
I told him thank you
and said we'd leave him alone.

15:44.068 --> 15:45.319
That's so great to hear.

15:47.321 --> 15:49.156
All my life, I've been on the run,

15:50.616 --> 15:52.701
and now I can put down real roots.

15:53.369 --> 15:56.121
I wanna have this little one
and take good care of it.

15:57.081 --> 15:58.290
This can be a tough world.

15:58.374 --> 16:01.794
And my child
might be headstrong like me.

16:03.045 --> 16:04.630
I just wanna give it a happy life.

16:09.426 --> 16:11.762
I have to say, you seem sort of down.
You okay?

16:13.347 --> 16:15.140
I had an argument with my husband.

16:15.766 --> 16:17.351
So you two really argue?

16:18.435 --> 16:20.479
He more or less said I was living in fear.

16:21.021 --> 16:23.983
That's pretty rich coming from a guy
who has basically never left his house.

16:24.066 --> 16:25.693
Like the pot calling the kettle black.

16:33.075 --> 16:35.536
You can stop looking for him.
Thought you might wanna know.

16:36.912 --> 16:37.746
Why though?

16:38.789 --> 16:39.790
Well, he's here.

16:40.290 --> 16:41.792
But have you two talked?

16:44.837 --> 16:48.090
Does it make you wanna run?
You're both in one place.

16:52.011 --> 16:53.971
I've never seen anyone
more scared than you.

17:05.441 --> 17:06.734
I mean, come on, man!

17:06.817 --> 17:09.820
She waited five years in that apartment
for a guy who might never come back.

17:10.404 --> 17:12.364
Wanna talk about boundaries for real?

17:12.448 --> 17:15.159
She has no idea
how dangerous this situation is.

17:15.242 --> 17:17.036
That woman can be so fucking stubborn.

17:17.911 --> 17:20.789
She's just… so selfish.

17:21.957 --> 17:25.669
She moved her stuff into my house,
and I'm not allowed to see that apartment?

17:26.628 --> 17:28.505
Does she need to
keep holding onto that shithole?

17:28.589 --> 17:29.965
That makes no sense at all, dude!

17:30.549 --> 17:33.761
Why are you freaking out, dude?
Not like it's a real marriage.

17:41.477 --> 17:43.645
I left early
to take care of a few things.

17:43.729 --> 17:46.231
About yesterday, that was uncalled-for.
I'm sorry.

17:48.067 --> 17:50.319
What? What did she say?

17:52.613 --> 17:53.864
Mainly, sorry.

17:53.947 --> 17:55.407
Well, there ya have it.

17:58.494 --> 17:59.787
I wasn't angry.

18:02.414 --> 18:03.791
I worry about In-ji.

18:12.508 --> 18:14.510
We've tightened security
throughout the area.

18:14.593 --> 18:16.261
And for the other building, sir?

18:17.513 --> 18:19.348
Just put a few CCTVs in his unit.

18:19.431 --> 18:22.392
Uh… Um, are you sure that works?

18:23.102 --> 18:24.603
Yes. Just do it.

18:46.208 --> 18:49.461
I think In-ji and I
are destined to perish side by side.

18:49.545 --> 18:51.588
I mean, if I can't have her, that is.

18:54.049 --> 18:55.342
That's a pretty good alternative.

19:08.522 --> 19:11.108
Apparently, it wasn't Do-ha's.
The blood.

19:12.401 --> 19:14.361
Ms. Do-dam saw him,
and she said he seemed fine.

19:15.404 --> 19:17.823
I guess we should be thankful
that he wasn't the victim.

19:19.741 --> 19:22.619
Come on. Don't you think
you should at least see his face?

19:23.996 --> 19:25.038
I'll take care of it.

19:25.122 --> 19:27.124
You'll take care of it? Right.

19:27.207 --> 19:29.835
When you first told me
about this marriage you're in,

19:30.377 --> 19:32.462
I figured you were desperate
and trying to survive,

19:32.546 --> 19:34.756
even though you were… really hurting.

19:35.883 --> 19:37.801
After my mom and dad separated,

19:38.343 --> 19:40.679
I… I was raised
living alone with my aunts.

19:40.762 --> 19:43.473
I lived like an orphan for five years,
feeling anxious.

19:45.058 --> 19:46.685
When I was in high school
and met you guys,

19:46.768 --> 19:48.270
I realized I finally had a family.

19:50.355 --> 19:51.940
Hye-yeong was an actual orphan,

19:52.733 --> 19:55.194
and you had cut ties with your mom
when you went off to college.

19:56.111 --> 19:57.487
And we all used to say,

19:57.571 --> 19:59.865
"We have each other,
so who needs a family or marriage?"

19:59.948 --> 20:02.242
We said that up until Hye-yeong died.

20:02.326 --> 20:04.453
Bitch ruined everything by dying.

20:05.120 --> 20:06.330
She abandoned us.

20:12.920 --> 20:15.589
You know, my greatest regret is
not going to that memorial.

20:16.340 --> 20:18.550
I missed it 'cause I had to
take care of my horrible aunt.

20:19.176 --> 20:21.553
She was a giant pain in the ass
right up until she died.

20:22.763 --> 20:24.139
My point is

20:24.223 --> 20:26.433
I'm the only family you've got
at this point.

20:26.516 --> 20:29.895
And you have no reason to be with that guy
if it's over between you and Do-ha.

20:31.063 --> 20:32.231
There's a contract.

20:32.856 --> 20:34.483
Oh, come on!

20:35.484 --> 20:36.944
You think I don't know you?

20:37.653 --> 20:39.821
When your eyes are red,
I can tell whether you cried

20:39.905 --> 20:41.907
'cause you're hurt
or 'cause you're pissed off.

20:41.990 --> 20:42.991
You were a walking corpse.

20:43.075 --> 20:45.035
Jeong-won shows up,
and you're alive again.

20:45.118 --> 20:46.662
Just admit you're in love!

20:50.999 --> 20:52.876
Either way,
there's nothing to worry about.

20:53.377 --> 20:55.170
Every contract expires in the end.

21:36.461 --> 21:39.006
If you haven't had supper,
we might as well eat together.

21:50.058 --> 21:51.727
What are you doing here, Seo-yeon?

21:53.395 --> 21:54.646
So where's In-ji?

21:57.524 --> 21:58.483
Not home, huh?

21:59.192 --> 22:01.320
Tell me why you came.

22:04.906 --> 22:06.908
Well, I have a question
to ask you, Jeong-won.

22:07.868 --> 22:10.287
What did you feel
the first time you saw In-ji?

22:15.000 --> 22:18.086
Haven't you ever wondered,
"Why did she pick her"?

22:26.845 --> 22:28.930
It's no coincidence. Can't be, huh?

22:31.975 --> 22:33.518
So what is it you're getting at?

22:37.731 --> 22:39.649
I didn't like those slippers you wore.

22:51.328 --> 22:52.371
Wait a sec.

23:00.087 --> 23:01.671
You're not actually gonna leave in those?

23:04.383 --> 23:05.675
Try these on.

23:24.152 --> 23:27.531
Everything became clear to me
once I saw In-ji's face at NM.

23:28.448 --> 23:31.451
Until then, I was repulsed
by the idea of staying with you.

23:32.411 --> 23:34.788
And when I saw her,
I suddenly knew I could work this out,

23:34.871 --> 23:36.123
and we could stay together.

23:38.250 --> 23:41.586
And that's the reason why you picked her,
so we could work things out together?

23:45.841 --> 23:48.593
I assumed I was the one who was shattered.
I was wrong.

23:50.011 --> 23:51.972
Now I'm realizing it was you all along.

23:54.224 --> 23:56.560
Then just end the marriage.
That one's on you.

23:58.061 --> 24:00.355
All it's gonna do is
push us further apart.

24:02.232 --> 24:03.233
I'll head out.

24:04.151 --> 24:06.111
Enjoy your dinner, sweetheart.

24:32.471 --> 24:34.598
You should be more than satisfied
with the alimony.

24:34.681 --> 24:37.100
We're liable for breach of contract,
after all.

24:37.184 --> 24:39.102
Well, how about a settlement instead?

24:39.603 --> 24:41.104
We could take you to court

24:41.188 --> 24:44.232
for pushing psychotropic medication
and filming illegally.

24:44.316 --> 24:45.442
Does that sound good?

24:46.318 --> 24:47.819
Why bullshit Jeong-won?

24:50.447 --> 24:52.032
He didn't seem to know yet.

24:52.908 --> 24:54.826
Because I don't know how
to explain the situation.

24:54.910 --> 24:56.161
I'm not sure yet.

24:58.330 --> 25:01.416
Don't get me wrong. I'm not hesitating
out of respect for you, okay?

25:02.083 --> 25:04.961
I guess you just don't want Jeong-won
to get hurt, do you?

25:05.504 --> 25:07.255
You're a fake. We know it's true.

25:07.839 --> 25:09.758
And yet you're scared
I'll take your place.

25:09.841 --> 25:11.301
Isn't that the reason we're here?

25:20.685 --> 25:23.188
No conditions
for a football match.

25:23.271 --> 25:25.357
You can see it
from the stadium as well

25:25.440 --> 25:27.692
if you look at
the front couple of rows of seats.

25:27.776 --> 25:28.985
Empty seats.

25:29.486 --> 25:32.113
Tuesday evening, cold and wet.

25:32.197 --> 25:35.325
No one's gonna be filling stadiums out
with games like this today…

25:36.159 --> 25:39.829
Been a while since soccer was on TV.
I'm surprised you can watch it right now.

25:41.039 --> 25:43.041
If you wanna watch with me,
would you just say it?

25:45.627 --> 25:47.379
Oh, sure. I bet you'd love that.

26:01.768 --> 26:04.312
Sorry I said
that you were immature earlier.

26:04.396 --> 26:06.523
And what about
the "me being selfish" part, huh?

26:07.107 --> 26:10.443
Let's call it even, okay?
I mean, you didn't handle it well either.

26:11.152 --> 26:13.863
Didn't you tell me
to go back to my mansion or something?

26:14.864 --> 26:16.866
And now here you are
in my place right now.

26:20.078 --> 26:21.371
You're holding a grudge?

26:21.955 --> 26:23.164
I just can't let it go.

26:24.666 --> 26:26.710
It's the first time
anyone's told me off, so…

26:31.131 --> 26:32.799
You know what? You were right.

26:36.761 --> 26:39.431
First, I was just doing it
purely out of spite.

26:39.514 --> 26:41.016
Then I got stubborn.

26:41.641 --> 26:44.269
Toward the end,
I was standing vigil at the apartment

26:44.769 --> 26:46.438
'cause it meant everything to me.

26:48.148 --> 26:50.817
After he left,
the apartment was like a hollow shell.

26:51.568 --> 26:53.528
I realized that I was the hollow shell.

26:56.615 --> 26:58.116
That's why I couldn't move on.

27:07.542 --> 27:09.502
You think you'll start over with Do-ha…

27:13.423 --> 27:14.924
once our contract is done?

27:16.926 --> 27:19.387
Are you just waiting
for this to end first? Hmm?

27:21.806 --> 27:23.391
I was wondering that as well.

27:25.018 --> 27:27.145
Do you think
you'll start over with Seo-yeon?

27:47.624 --> 27:49.167
You two aren't compatible.

27:50.168 --> 27:53.463
Both of you know it,
and you're… lying to yourselves.

27:54.547 --> 27:56.007
Well, I chose Jeong-won.

27:59.052 --> 28:02.263
Listen. You need this marriage, okay?
It's the best thing for you.

28:03.598 --> 28:04.474
Is that right?

28:04.974 --> 28:06.643
We're equally spiteful.

28:09.521 --> 28:11.648
At least tell me
you'll honor the contract.

28:11.731 --> 28:14.025
It's not your fault
that we're terminating it early.

28:14.109 --> 28:15.735
They will know that, okay?

28:16.236 --> 28:17.737
You think I'm worried about that?

28:18.863 --> 28:20.782
What's with this
self-destructive attitude?

28:20.865 --> 28:22.367
Why are you being so reckless?

28:27.122 --> 28:27.956
Get over here.

28:35.296 --> 28:36.214
Would you?

29:30.477 --> 29:32.896
I guess… we should meet up.

29:40.111 --> 29:41.446
Let's grab a bite.

30:01.132 --> 30:03.009
Hey, I'm gonna head over to the unit.

30:04.928 --> 30:06.179
Will it take a while?

30:07.472 --> 30:08.389
Uh, no.

30:10.809 --> 30:11.976
Have a good time, okay?

30:56.604 --> 30:58.231
I made you some doenjang jjigae.

30:58.815 --> 30:59.732
It's ready now.

31:00.567 --> 31:01.442
Take a seat.

31:15.498 --> 31:16.416
Go for it.

31:28.011 --> 31:29.846
I think I must've over-seasoned it.

31:35.476 --> 31:37.145
Oh, I made egg rolls as well.

31:47.113 --> 31:49.073
There's kimchi too. I should go get it.

31:49.157 --> 31:50.825
Aren't you a little

31:52.327 --> 31:54.829
curious what my meals look like
without you?

31:58.249 --> 32:01.502
I knew I should've put in less doenjang.
It's because this stuff is homemade.

32:01.586 --> 32:02.587
Hey, In-ji,

32:03.588 --> 32:04.797
stop it, all right?

32:08.343 --> 32:10.762
Everything started going wrong
the moment I met you.

32:11.596 --> 32:13.097
Your mother wasn't at fault.

32:13.806 --> 32:14.766
You were.

32:21.230 --> 32:22.732
We were happy as we were.

32:23.650 --> 32:25.777
There wasn't some need for me to change.

32:25.860 --> 32:28.112
And it felt like we didn't need
other people's approval.

32:33.493 --> 32:35.578
Then you ruined my life
with your selfishness.

32:36.788 --> 32:38.456
Do you still feel like blaming me

32:39.415 --> 32:42.043
for leaving you alone here
and running off by myself?

32:44.087 --> 32:44.921
You're wrong.

32:47.715 --> 32:49.634
I really thought I might be a monster.

32:50.426 --> 32:52.887
After I cut ties with everyone
and I was boarding the flight,

32:54.514 --> 32:56.683
I felt like
I was losing my entire identity.

32:58.476 --> 33:01.270
I have this question, "Who am I?"
And I wanted to ask you.

33:04.816 --> 33:06.401
But I was so afraid to see you.

33:08.319 --> 33:09.779
I simply could not do it.

33:11.322 --> 33:13.324
I wanted to blame you for everything,

33:14.575 --> 33:16.035
but even that hurt me so bad.

33:18.413 --> 33:20.289
Why'd you do this to me? Why, In-ji?

33:25.044 --> 33:28.172
In-ji, why'd you make it
so I couldn't bring myself to see you?

33:43.104 --> 33:46.691
I thought I wouldn't be able to breathe
if I ever saw you again.

33:51.237 --> 33:52.530
Turns out I can.

33:57.201 --> 33:59.704
You know,
I felt horrible about what I did to you.

34:00.747 --> 34:03.374
See, I contemplated killing myself
and killing you.

34:04.876 --> 34:06.586
Actually, most nights, I prayed

34:08.171 --> 34:10.965
that I wouldn't wake up in the morning,
that I'd be wiped out.

34:11.924 --> 34:13.801
Every single day was a living hell,

34:13.885 --> 34:16.387
and yet I stayed here by myself
and stuck it out.

34:19.640 --> 34:20.516
I'd think,

34:21.684 --> 34:23.394
"Wait a little longer."

34:23.478 --> 34:25.938
"He'll come back and sit down
like any other day."

34:26.439 --> 34:27.607
Day two.

34:28.441 --> 34:29.609
Day three.

34:29.692 --> 34:30.693
More days.

34:31.194 --> 34:32.111
Hundreds.

34:34.363 --> 34:37.408
As time went by and I waited,
my wish started to change.

34:38.242 --> 34:40.453
I hoped you'd come back
just so it would end.

34:41.996 --> 34:44.499
I knew I didn't have the strength
to end it myself.

34:45.374 --> 34:47.293
And I prayed for you to return.

34:49.045 --> 34:51.297
Like I was begging for a merciful death.

34:54.759 --> 34:55.760
Do-ha…

34:59.097 --> 35:00.890
you were gone for so long.

35:03.017 --> 35:05.394
How could you hide from me for five years?

35:05.478 --> 35:06.354
How could you…

35:10.066 --> 35:12.443
I mean, you could've told me something.

35:13.778 --> 35:16.989
All you had to do is reach out and say,

35:17.073 --> 35:18.950
"This marriage is over for good!"

35:35.758 --> 35:36.926
I know I should have…

35:41.222 --> 35:43.349
had this conversation with you years ago.

35:46.352 --> 35:48.646
And I really needed
to hear this years ago.

35:52.024 --> 35:53.442
In-ji, I'm so sorry.

35:55.027 --> 35:55.903
In-ji…

36:07.790 --> 36:08.749
I'm grateful…

36:13.004 --> 36:15.298
you carried on and didn't choose suicide.

36:34.984 --> 36:36.903
- Okay. Like that? One.
- That's it.

36:36.986 --> 36:38.362
- And two…
- And two… Hey!

36:38.446 --> 36:39.739
- Hang on.
- Whoa!

36:39.822 --> 36:41.532
Wait, no!Whoa!

36:43.075 --> 36:45.203
- That's it.
- You're supposed to hold me up!

36:46.746 --> 36:47.580
That hurt.

36:47.663 --> 36:49.665
You're doing the dishes?
You get a gold star!

36:49.749 --> 36:53.377
Oh, great. Hey, let's do that tofu stew.
The spicy kind?

36:53.461 --> 36:55.713
Oh my God. Soft tofu stew
sounds incredible right now.

36:55.796 --> 36:56.881
Makgeolli?

36:57.882 --> 36:59.550
- Bright little fins.
- Look at her.

37:01.594 --> 37:04.013
Why don't you try
putting yourself in my shoes, okay?

37:04.096 --> 37:06.057
When the hell are you gonna grow up?

37:06.641 --> 37:08.184
This isn't cute, Do-ha.

37:08.267 --> 37:10.478
You're probably looking for sympathy,
but I can't do that

37:10.561 --> 37:12.939
'cause you're driving me crazy here.
Just admit you're afraid!

37:13.022 --> 37:13.981
You're

37:15.650 --> 37:17.151
just like your mother, you know that?

37:38.506 --> 37:40.383
Where are you?

37:40.466 --> 37:42.218
I'm worried about you. Come home.

38:19.213 --> 38:20.715
Did you have a good time?

39:42.963 --> 39:45.925
Did you break down… because of him?

39:47.927 --> 39:48.969
Oh, no.

39:50.596 --> 39:52.390
I saw you and, before I knew it…

39:57.395 --> 40:00.314
Mostly, I felt…
I don't know. I felt happy.

40:03.442 --> 40:05.027
You cried like a baby

40:05.986 --> 40:07.154
'cause I was there?

40:11.742 --> 40:13.285
I was happy to see you…

40:14.912 --> 40:15.913
cry like that.

40:53.576 --> 40:54.660
So what do you like?

40:58.747 --> 41:00.124
I mean, side dishes.

41:01.959 --> 41:03.586
I don't really have preferences.

41:05.588 --> 41:06.714
Any music?

41:10.217 --> 41:14.263
Do you like film scores and… stuff?

41:18.309 --> 41:19.727
Wanna come see me at work?

41:23.147 --> 41:24.148
That sounds good.

41:25.024 --> 41:26.609
You let me know a time. Is tomorrow too--

41:26.692 --> 41:27.860
That's great, In-ji.

41:30.321 --> 41:31.155
Okay.

41:36.827 --> 41:38.496
Kids, it's time to eat.

41:38.996 --> 41:41.957
Hwan, Gwan. Get over here.
Your mom's tired, all right?

41:44.001 --> 41:45.461
Boys, sit down!

41:46.170 --> 41:47.463
Get your butts over here.

41:56.514 --> 41:58.182
Hey, stop! That's mine.

41:58.265 --> 41:59.391
No, it's mine!

41:59.475 --> 42:02.186
Whoa, hey! Hold still, hold still,
or you're gonna get hurt.

42:03.395 --> 42:04.897
You think I should start working again?

42:05.731 --> 42:08.609
- You're hogging it!
- I don't know if I'm cut out for this.

42:10.027 --> 42:12.363
Imagine hiring tutors
and sending the kids to private school.

42:12.446 --> 42:14.573
Then throw in a nanny
to pick them up afterward.

42:15.074 --> 42:16.700
We'd be in the red, no doubt.

42:16.784 --> 42:18.661
- Give it here!
- I don't want to.

42:18.744 --> 42:22.122
- Give it back. It's mine.
- I know. It's basically hell.

42:22.206 --> 42:25.084
- Come on!
- Ugh! You're being so unfair!

42:25.167 --> 42:26.418
All done. Go on.

42:26.502 --> 42:27.419
Let's go!

42:28.963 --> 42:30.339
Let's go, let's go!

42:49.858 --> 42:52.820
Are you crying 'cause I wanna get a job?

42:53.404 --> 42:56.282
Uh… Jesus, time flies, huh?

42:57.283 --> 42:58.617
The kids' toenails.

42:58.701 --> 43:00.828
They used to be so soft,
but now they're getting hard.

43:01.745 --> 43:03.747
It feels different when I clip them now.

43:06.667 --> 43:08.294
They're growing into little adults.

43:08.377 --> 43:11.547
They're gonna start slamming the door
on us when they're teenagers.

43:12.840 --> 43:14.425
It's just getting to me.

43:16.677 --> 43:20.306
There, there. It's okay, honey.
We'll always have each other, right?

43:30.232 --> 43:34.153
Let's grow old together, honey.
I love you.

43:34.862 --> 43:35.946
You too.

43:56.925 --> 43:59.511
The body's been
decomposing for a while.

44:00.679 --> 44:02.222
The killer put a sign on the shutters.

44:02.306 --> 44:04.350
The owner left
to study abroad for a month.

44:04.433 --> 44:07.061
Crazy bastard murders a woman,
then prints this crap out here.

44:07.144 --> 44:08.812
Hey, what about the CCTV?

44:08.896 --> 44:12.232
We got our hands on
the footage from the alleyway.

44:12.316 --> 44:15.527
Unfortunately, this bastard
wiped the pharmacy footage.

44:15.611 --> 44:18.906
Her neck's been snapped. Clean job.

44:19.573 --> 44:20.991
Not a drop of blood.

44:21.575 --> 44:23.619
The blood we found
has to be the killer's, then.

44:24.244 --> 44:25.371
Send it to forensics.

44:25.454 --> 44:27.998
Once they get DNA results,
run it against ex-cons in the system.

44:28.082 --> 44:29.333
You got it, sir.

44:35.547 --> 44:38.550
Eom Tae-seong
has been following Han Jeong-won.

44:39.259 --> 44:41.512
They've been around
the same locations lately.

44:42.262 --> 44:44.139
It doesn't bode well for the future.

44:46.975 --> 44:48.435
I've notified the company.

44:50.187 --> 44:51.313
I understand.

45:51.165 --> 45:52.291
Hi. Hello?

45:56.336 --> 45:57.171
NOH IN-JI

45:57.254 --> 45:58.297
She actually picked up.

46:00.716 --> 46:01.633
In-ji?

46:04.219 --> 46:05.262
Meet me soon.

46:05.846 --> 46:07.556
Oh, sure.

46:08.724 --> 46:09.767
When? Uh…

46:10.726 --> 46:11.977
Oh…

46:33.207 --> 46:39.213
NOH IN-JI:
CAFE CAVIAR AT 2 P.M.

47:31.598 --> 47:33.141
There's something I'd like to know.

47:34.268 --> 47:35.185
Of course.

47:36.645 --> 47:40.107
Do you harass me and watch my every move
and stalk me just 'cause you like it?

47:42.860 --> 47:45.070
You're probably the only person I can ask.

47:49.157 --> 47:52.411
One thing kept bothering me
while I was in the mental institution.

47:53.495 --> 47:56.498
"Noh In-ji deserves a great life.
Why is she cruel to herself?"

47:57.124 --> 47:58.083
"That's what I'll do."

47:58.166 --> 48:00.586
"I'll tell everyone about
her marriage to Do-ha."

48:01.795 --> 48:04.840
Once I decided that, I felt calmer,
like my head was suddenly clear.

48:04.923 --> 48:06.091
It just felt new.

48:08.886 --> 48:10.512
I guess it was bliss.

48:15.893 --> 48:17.352
And now let me ask you.

48:18.520 --> 48:20.063
Your wedding contract's in the trunk?

48:22.316 --> 48:24.860
I mean, people might not believe me,
but they have to believe that.

48:24.943 --> 48:26.361
It's material proof.

48:26.445 --> 48:28.655
Once this story gets leaked
to the Internet and the press,

48:28.739 --> 48:31.074
it could be a huge sensation, you know?

48:32.784 --> 48:35.746
I actually paid a visit to the flat
'cause I thought it was there.

48:38.040 --> 48:39.374
Took a knife in the thigh.

48:40.000 --> 48:41.251
It was Seo Do-ha.

48:43.503 --> 48:47.341
Man, that guy was such a loser.
He's changed.

48:50.260 --> 48:52.638
Because of him,
I had to murder a woman that night.

48:55.974 --> 48:57.893
Who did you kill? What are you saying?

49:02.814 --> 49:03.982
Why do I disgust you?

49:05.442 --> 49:06.818
You're that bewildered?

49:11.865 --> 49:12.908
I'm done with this.

49:13.951 --> 49:15.202
I have things to do.

49:29.800 --> 49:31.760
Right, let's cut it there.

49:32.803 --> 49:34.680
Get rid of that.

49:34.763 --> 49:36.264
Sounds good to me.

49:36.348 --> 49:37.557
Lower it a little.

49:46.650 --> 49:48.318
Uh, he's acting weird.

49:54.074 --> 49:56.827
Work five more minutes, then go.
I'll take care of the rest.

49:57.828 --> 49:59.037
That track sounds great.

50:00.497 --> 50:02.874
What is going on with that guy?

50:02.958 --> 50:04.167
Good news, I bet.

50:08.880 --> 50:11.008
Hey, I'll be
at the parking garage soon.

50:12.551 --> 50:14.720
Wait right there.
I'll be down in a sec.

50:28.734 --> 50:30.819
Tell me what you're doing here right now.

50:31.486 --> 50:34.281
It's just…
you never answered the question.

50:38.452 --> 50:39.995
Why do I disgust you?

50:42.039 --> 50:46.126
I mean, you hated me… from day one,
and I hadn't done anything to you yet.

50:46.209 --> 50:47.919
We barely knew each other, In-ji.

50:48.712 --> 50:50.589
But you hated me
as soon as you laid eyes on me.

50:50.672 --> 50:51.798
So tell me why.

50:52.382 --> 50:54.051
That wasn't true with Jeong-won.

51:00.682 --> 51:02.267
Speaking of which,

51:03.101 --> 51:05.979
would you give me attention, In-ji,
if I murdered Jeong-won?

51:09.566 --> 51:10.484
I'll do it.

51:11.568 --> 51:14.154
You're not going to hurt Jeong-won.
I won't let you.

51:18.867 --> 51:20.035
Then just tell me.

51:20.535 --> 51:22.662
Why are you choosing Jeong-won?

51:23.163 --> 51:24.539
Let go.

51:32.672 --> 51:34.299
Hmm?

51:35.342 --> 51:36.426
Say it. Why are you--

51:36.510 --> 51:37.969
Back off!

51:50.732 --> 51:52.609
Crazy piece of shit!

51:52.692 --> 51:53.610
Die!

51:54.653 --> 51:57.197
Die… motherfucker!

51:57.280 --> 51:58.323
Die!

51:58.406 --> 52:00.117
- Fucker!
- Jeong-won, stop it!

52:00.700 --> 52:01.785
Wait! Stop!

52:02.327 --> 52:03.620
Jeong-won, stop!

52:59.676 --> 53:01.720
You told me you went
to shooting ranges with your dad,

53:01.803 --> 53:03.180
but this is insane.

53:03.263 --> 53:05.974
Didn't you say he'd drag you along,
and you didn't wanna go, huh?

53:06.558 --> 53:07.392
What's going on?

53:07.475 --> 53:09.895
'Cause after that, didn't you say
you wouldn't pick up a gun?

53:11.438 --> 53:14.191
My God! Do you still have
that gun in your house?

53:17.194 --> 53:19.321
That thing looked so badass, right?
Your dad's gun.

53:20.739 --> 53:22.324
And it's not registered, right?

53:23.783 --> 53:24.826
Have you

53:26.161 --> 53:27.871
ever thought of killing anyone?

53:29.456 --> 53:32.584
Hell yeah. A lot of times,
I wanna blow your head off.

53:36.963 --> 53:38.548
You really wanna kill someone?

53:46.097 --> 53:49.726
CONFRONTATION
WITH DEPUTY MANAGER NOH IN-JI

53:56.816 --> 53:58.610
Deputy Manager Noh In-ji is here.

53:58.693 --> 54:00.195
Okay, show her inside.

54:02.113 --> 54:04.199
PHYSICAL ALTERCATION
WITH CLIENT HAN JEONG-WON

54:17.379 --> 54:20.298
If this is about Eom Tae-seong,
we're coming up with a solution right now.

54:21.424 --> 54:23.843
I know. I want to discuss my employment.

54:26.680 --> 54:29.099
Once I finish the current marriage
I've been assigned to,

54:29.599 --> 54:30.976
I'd like to leave the company.

54:32.686 --> 54:36.147
So does this…
just have to do with Mr. Seo?

54:36.773 --> 54:37.774
Oh, no.

54:38.566 --> 54:40.402
As an employee, I'm not productive.

54:42.237 --> 54:44.572
I just think that, at this point,
I'm quite unfit for this.

54:44.656 --> 54:46.074
That's just silly.

54:46.783 --> 54:49.494
No other single NM employee
gets these sorts of results.

54:52.038 --> 54:54.457
I think it's best for the company
if I quit right now.

54:55.125 --> 54:58.461
Eom Tae-seong could put
the company at risk if I don't leave.

54:59.212 --> 55:02.632
Knowing him, it could be
that if I move on, he won't be an issue.

55:02.716 --> 55:04.342
If that's what's on your mind,

55:04.843 --> 55:06.761
we'll do everything in our power
to stop him.

55:06.845 --> 55:08.388
I've made my decision already.

55:11.224 --> 55:12.934
I do appreciate your mentorship.

55:29.075 --> 55:30.618
Mmm…

55:34.789 --> 55:37.625
Oh! That's potent. Vending machine.

55:38.168 --> 55:39.711
Ah, it's great.

55:39.794 --> 55:42.505
Yirgacheffe's always been
a favorite of mine.

55:44.215 --> 55:45.425
Here you are.

55:45.508 --> 55:48.720
The CEO's coming to see
someone like me 'cause In-ji's quitting.

55:51.890 --> 55:53.850
Do you have any idea why she's quitting?

55:54.434 --> 55:56.353
I guess it's because of Tae-seong.

55:57.479 --> 55:59.939
If you killed him,
things wouldn't have gotten crazy.

56:02.108 --> 56:03.068
Just kidding.

56:03.151 --> 56:05.987
God, you look like
a monk with freaky eyes.

56:08.865 --> 56:11.701
Long before this,
she… had issues with Tae-seong.

56:12.202 --> 56:14.371
Naturally, I figured
there was another reason.

56:14.454 --> 56:17.707
I think it's… over
between her and the flat owner.

56:18.291 --> 56:21.961
So that means
your business is to create good matches,

56:22.796 --> 56:26.800
but those relationships still take
some devotion from both parties to work.

56:26.883 --> 56:28.968
It's not just a contract.

56:29.886 --> 56:31.596
They're bound to either hate each other

56:31.679 --> 56:35.433
or bond and develop
a real attraction and feelings.

56:37.227 --> 56:40.230
I'm sorry. You're saying…
she's doing this for Jeong-won,

56:40.313 --> 56:41.314
not Eom Tae-seong?

56:41.398 --> 56:43.316
Take it from someone experienced.

56:43.400 --> 56:45.402
I married three times
and divorced three times.

56:46.069 --> 56:48.863
Couples can put up with material problems
like money and career issues,

56:48.947 --> 56:51.491
but nobody will put up
with a lack of love.

56:51.991 --> 56:54.077
It's phony, but people would

56:54.869 --> 56:56.830
have a tough time
holding back their feelings.

56:56.913 --> 56:58.331
They're people, after all.

56:59.999 --> 57:02.585
You know In-ji. How do you think
she'd deal with this?

57:03.753 --> 57:08.258
You're saying she might be leaving us
'cause… she's in love with an NM client?

57:14.139 --> 57:15.432
God, that's bitter.

58:21.623 --> 58:23.124
MR. KIM

58:26.377 --> 58:27.504
Hello, Mr. Kim.

58:52.487 --> 58:56.032
The CCTV technician we hired
came across it during the installation.

58:56.866 --> 58:58.868
He said an expert must have put them in.

59:00.036 --> 59:01.621
Shall I take care of it?

59:34.404 --> 59:36.030
You need to get home right away.

59:37.198 --> 59:39.617
I think Jeong-won knows
you're watching now.

59:54.966 --> 59:56.884
OPEN DOOR

01:00:13.276 --> 01:00:15.069
Let's pretend you never found them, okay?

01:00:17.405 --> 01:00:18.364
Where is it?

01:00:48.311 --> 01:00:51.648
RECENTLY ACCESSED
PAST SEVEN DAYS

01:02:05.304 --> 01:02:08.099
RECENT CALLS
NOH IN-JI

01:02:08.182 --> 01:02:10.351
Listen, we've examined
the gallery on Tae-seong's phone,

01:02:10.852 --> 01:02:13.312
and there were
a whole lot of pictures of you in there.

01:02:18.776 --> 01:02:20.194
Why didn't you call the cops on him?

01:02:24.407 --> 01:02:25.408
Oh, I did.

01:02:26.367 --> 01:02:27.326
A few times.

01:02:28.453 --> 01:02:30.413
I was told
there was nothing that could be done

01:02:30.496 --> 01:02:32.123
unless someone died or got hurt.

01:02:45.636 --> 01:02:46.971
Took a knife in the thigh.

01:02:47.555 --> 01:02:48.890
It was Seo Do-ha.

01:02:48.973 --> 01:02:51.434
Because of him,
I had to murder a woman that night.

01:02:52.435 --> 01:02:55.938
We found Tae-seong's blood
at the scene. Plenty of his prints too.

01:02:56.647 --> 01:03:00.443
But… even though that pharmacy case
is all wrapped up now,

01:03:00.943 --> 01:03:02.779
and we're not gonna be able
to prosecute him,

01:03:02.862 --> 01:03:06.324
we still have a duty to catch criminals,
even if a bad guy got killed here.

01:03:10.369 --> 01:03:12.747
We've gone over
all the places Tae-seong went.

01:03:13.414 --> 01:03:15.917
We noticed he was always around
people in your orbit.

01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:17.668
He broke into an apartment

01:03:17.752 --> 01:03:20.254
and assaulted Han Jeong-won, and so on…

01:03:24.008 --> 01:03:25.051
Okay. And?

01:03:28.679 --> 01:03:31.349
I've been thinking.
Who would have the motive to kill him?

01:03:31.432 --> 01:03:34.268
Who hated the guy
to the extent they'd want him gone?

01:03:38.022 --> 01:03:38.981
So, In-ji,

01:03:40.107 --> 01:03:41.526
tell us where you were that day.

01:03:54.705 --> 01:03:55.957
On the water.
